digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "N13" [label="(7,0,0) DIP variants for optical phase retrieval force physics consistency by minimizing loss function between estimated and actual measurements"];
  "N14" [label="(8,0,0) Typical DIP-type DNNs rely on forward mapping function with analytical model describing physical evolution process"];
  "N19" [label="(12,0,0) Analytical models can only be applied where strongly optical scattering is absent"];
  "N2" [label="(2,0,0) Supervised learning excels at learning complex relationships from large input-output data pairs in an end-to-end manner"];
  "N20" [label="(13,0,0) Many optical systems lack analytical theory, with wave scattering systems having non-negligible backward scattering as typical examples"];
  "N24" [label="(14,0,0) Physics-enhanced DNNs based on analytical theory are inapplicable in systems without analytical theory"];
  "N27" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: Given current methods are inapplicable (case), and if methods are inapplicable then a gap exists (rule), therefore there is a gap in solving phase retrieval for scattering systems without analytical theory"];
  "N28" [label="(15,0,0) Leveraging DIP concept for optical phase retrieval over scattering medium remains alluring but challenging"];
  "N29" [label="(11,0,0) Generating estimated results using empirical model based on real system response, where model must be differentiable for backpropagation, is a promising but open attempt for untrained network updates"];
  "N3" [label="(3,0,0) Large-scale labeled data and extensive training are indispensable prerequisites for supervised learning, which are time-consuming and energy-intensive"];
  "N33" [label="(17,0,0) Experimentally calibrated empirical transmission matrix describing forward mapping of MIMO system is integrated into DNN for backpropagation"];
  "N35" [label="(19,0,0) Unlike analytical theory predicting full evolution, empirical model resembles partial experimental measurement providing insights for DENN update"];
  "N38" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Given empirical TM describes forward mapping experimentally (case), and empirical models work without full theory (common), therefore empirical TM can replace analytical models for network training"];
  "N39" [label="(20,0,0) Need for labeled data and training can be eliminated by integrating empirical model of opaque system with convnet"];
  "N44" [label="(21,0,0) Seeing through multimode fiber and ground glass achieved using single-shot speckle intensity"];
  "N49" [label="(25,0,0) Empirical TM can be calibrated for different scattering media, making neural network combination applicable for various media"];
  "N8" [label="(5,0,0) Physics-enhanced DNNs have been proposed to overcome the big data challenge by integrating physical prior into neural networks"];
  "N9" [label="(6,0,0) Untrained neural networks inspired by deep image prior have been widely used in metrology, holography, and imaging"];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Develop and evaluate an untrained physics-enhanced deep neural network that incorporates an experimentally calibrated differentiable empirical transmission matrix as its forward model for single-shot optical phase retrieval through scattering media such as multimode fiber and ground glass, reducing reliance on analytical theory and large labeled training datasets.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When analytical forward models and labeled datasets are limiting, a differentiable experimentally calibrated empirical forward model can supply physics-like constraints for untrained neural-network phase retrieval."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Substantial data and training requirements in supervised deep learning motivate physics-enhanced DNNs that integrate physical priors to address the big-data challenge."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Untrained neural networks inspired by deep image prior are established in optical applications, including contexts related to optical phase retrieval."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) DIP-type DNNs that rely on analytical forward models are limited to optical systems where the physical evolution can be analytically described."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) DIP-type optical phase-retrieval methods enforce physics consistency through analytical forward-mapping models in the loss function."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Because DIP-type optical phase-retrieval methods rely on analytical forward models, they are not directly applicable where no adequate analytical theory is available."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) Scattering optical systems, including systems with non-negligible backward scattering, are examples where analytical theory may be lacking or restricted."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) Strong optical scattering restricts the applicability of analytical models."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) The reliance of many physics-enhanced DNNs on analytical descriptions limits their applicability to scattering systems where such descriptions are unavailable or unreliable."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) If phase-retrieval methods depend on analytical models that are inapplicable to systems without adequate analytical theory, then a methodological gap remains for such systems."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) Physics-enhanced DNNs based on analytical theory are inapplicable in systems without analytical theory."];
  "R20" [label="(0,0,0) A gap in phase retrieval for scattering systems without analytical theory, together with the challenge of leveraging DIP over scattering media, defines the key problem setting."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) A differentiable empirical model based on real system response is a promising route for updating untrained networks in scattering-media phase retrieval."];
  "R22" [label="(0,0,0) An experimentally calibrated empirical transmission matrix can describe the forward input-output mapping of a scattering MIMO system and be integrated into a DNN for backpropagation."];
  "R23" [label="(0,0,0) Empirical models can provide experimentally measured guidance for DENN updates without requiring a full analytical description of the physical evolution."];
  "R25" [label="(0,0,0) Integrating a calibrated empirical transmission matrix or empirical model with a convnet enables backpropagation-based updates for opaque systems."];
  "R27" [label="(0,0,0) DENN shows a favorable performance pattern across the reported multimode-fiber and ground-glass demonstrations, while broader media applicability depends on empirical-TM calibration."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Integrating an empirical model of an opaque system with a convnet supports untrained-network updates without requiring labeled training data for that system."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) DENN is demonstrated for the tested scattering media, including multimode fiber and ground glass, with single-shot measurement and improved fidelity, motivating evaluation across calibratable scattering media."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Supervised learning for inverse problems relies on large input-output or labeled data pairs and extensive training."];
